  "response_text": "The __io_putchar function is used to redirect output from functions (ex. printf) to a specific output device. For embedded systems, printf(), for example, doesn\u2019t know where it should be sending its output by default (there is no screen or console on a computer), and so by defining __io_putchar, you\u2019re essentially telling the system how to handle each character that printf() wats to print. The function is needed to make standard C functions work properly on microcontrollers.\\n",
